Attribution

The starting point for the recall ranking formula -- its semantic / keyword /
entity split -- is mem0 (https://github.com/mem0ai/mem0), which is licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0 and permits it. The three further signals
(reinforcement, recency, level), the constant denominator and the weights
themselves are this project's own.

The derivation is cited where it is implemented:

    modules/aimon-memory-core/src/main/java/at/aimon/memory/core/model/FusionWeights.java
    modules/aimon-memory-recall/src/main/java/at/aimon/memory/recall/FusionRanker.java

and the reasoning that draws the line is recorded in
docs/adr/0005-agpl-boundary.md.

No source code, prompt text, structured-output schema or SQL from any other
project is included here. Prompts, schemas and SQL are written from the
specification in docs/spec/, which is what ADR 0005 exists to keep true.

================================================================================
Third-party dependencies

Third-party libraries are resolved at build time and none of them are
redistributed in this repository. Their coordinates and versions are declared in
gradle/libs.versions.toml and in the Spring Boot and Testcontainers platforms
imported by buildSrc/src/main/kotlin/aimon.java-conventions.gradle.kts. Each
carries its own license and, where it has one, its own NOTICE file; both apply to
any distribution that bundles them.
